  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Math-43",
    "project": "Math",
    "summary": "Statistics.setVarianceImpl makes getStandardDeviation produce NaN",
    "description": "Invoking SummaryStatistics.setVarianceImpl(new Variance(true/false) makes getStandardDeviation produce NaN. The code to reproduce it:\n\nint\n[] scores = {1, 2, 3, 4};\nSummaryStatistics stats = \nnew\nSummaryStatistics();\nstats.setVarianceImpl(\nnew\nVariance(\nfalse\n)); \n//use \n\"population variance\"\n\nfor\n(\nint\ni : scores) {\nstats.addValue(i);\n}\n\ndouble\nsd = stats.getStandardDeviation();\n\nSystem\n.out.println(sd);\n\nA workaround suggested by Mikkel is:\n\ndouble\nsd = FastMath.sqrt(stats.getSecondMoment() / stats.getN());"
  },
